{"class": "no-cause", "verdict": "patch", "citations": [{"kind": "instruction", "path": "/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/cli.py", "symbol": "counsel help: read-only; commits nothing\u2014the caller commits, as with every stage", "ruling_id": null}, {"kind": "mechanism", "path": "/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/build.py", "symbol": "cmd_build foreign-commit check", "ruling_id": null}, {"kind": "guard", "path": "/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_counsel.py", "symbol": "test_counsel_ask_reads_the_latest_record_even_when_it_passed", "ruling_id": null}], "proposal": {"ruling_text": null, "patch": null, "question": null, "issue": {"title": "A counsel status question can poison an active build with a foreign commit", "body": "Severity: high / Provenance: product\n\n## Problem\n\nItem 229\u2019s executor committed the requested implementation at `15a774515f5a`. While build-01 was still active, `counsel --ask \"how is it going so far?\"` wrote counsel-01 and the driver committed it at `24aed171c5ec`. On the executor\u2019s next return, `cmd_build` correctly found that driver-authored commit between `start_sha` and HEAD and refused the build as `no-cause`.\n\nThe operator\u2019s read-only status question therefore changed the active build\u2019s HEAD and invalidated an otherwise executor-authored build. The green forge checks do not cure this race, and the selected-test failure does not explain the recorded refusal.\n\n## Retires\n\nA read-only counsel/status inquiry, or transport of its record, being able to introduce a foreign commit into an active build\u2019s commit range.\n\n## Change\n\nMake counsel/status recording and transport unable to mutate the checkout observed by an active build. Use an isolated transport worktree or defer the counsel-record commit until the active stage has produced its record. Preserve the build\u2019s foreign-author guard; driver commits must not be silently exempted from it.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Start a two-iteration build whose first iteration creates an executor-authored commit and whose second iteration is still running.\n- Run `attavo counsel N --ask \"how is it going so far?\"` and transport its record during that interval.\n- The active build\u2019s HEAD and executor commit range remain unchanged by the counsel operation.\n- The build is not refused for the counsel record and can pass after its gates pass.\n- The counsel record is eventually committed by the driver without being lost.\n- An actual non-executor commit introduced into the build\u2019s range remains refused by the existing authorship guard."}}}